# LinuxCNC's servo thread with timing jitter (host main.c lcnc_jitter): the
# updates arrive up to 2 rt ticks (0.4 ms) early or late, then also 5 % of
# them lost, while the burn-in axis jogs at 100 rad/s. The drive follows
# without a link fault (sserial0.error) or a drive fault, but its following
# error grows (DEBUGNOTES 2026-11-11, Open): steady 0.0006 rad, +-0.2 ms
# 0.018, +-0.4 ms 0.041, 5 % lost 0.038, 20 % lost 0.10 (a lost update is
# taken as a double step: ~one period's travel, 0.1 rad at 100 rad/s).
# The limits hold today's numbers, so a change either way shows.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 100
run 1
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.0002 0.5
lcnc_jitter 2 0 7
run 0.2
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.0002 0.5
lcnc_jitter 2 5 7
run 0.2
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.0002 0.5
sserial0.error
fault0.fault
lcnc_stats
@expect sserial0.error == 0
@expect fault0.fault == 0
@expect max|pid0.pos_error[1:2500]| < 0.002
@expect max|pid0.pos_error[2501:5000]| < 0.06
@expect max|pid0.pos_error[5001:7500]| < 0.06
